@startuml
actor "Platform Engineer" as PE
actor Developer
participant Console
participant Orchestrator
participant "Repository host" as Git
participant Fleet
database PostgreSQL
PE -> Console : Discover/verify CD and Git policy
Console -> Orchestrator : Set verified platform default (CAS)
Orchestrator -> PostgreSQL : Save default binding/version
Developer -> Console : Create Application
Console -> Orchestrator : Name/subdomain only
Orchestrator -> PostgreSQL : Create Application/Environments and pin default
Developer -> Console : Preview
Console -> Orchestrator : Plan pinned workload/dependencies (no Git writes)
Developer -> Console : Deploy reviewed revision
Orchestrator -> PostgreSQL : Admit operation and reserve application repository
Orchestrator -> Git : Observe deterministic repo; create private if absent
Git --> Orchestrator : Exact repository ID / branch
Orchestrator -> PostgreSQL : Acknowledge allocation (CAS)
Orchestrator -> Git : Publish <root>/<env>/<workload>/<phase> + metadata
Orchestrator -> Fleet : CAS one Application GitRepo SHA; preserve sibling tree pins
Fleet --> Orchestrator : Observation / UID inventory
Orchestrator -> PostgreSQL : Acknowledge admitted revision
@enduml
